      "body": "## What\r\n\r\n`test_nixl_transfer_engine_e2e.py` (AMD disaggregation stage) no longer passes `--disaggregation-ib-device` to the NIXL servers. It uses `configure_nixl_pd_backend`, like the other NIXL PD tests, so UCX keeps the fixture's `UCX_NET_DEVICES=rdma0:1,rdma4:1,lo`.\r\n\r\n## Why\r\n\r\nSince #43482, both NIXL servers fail in `createBackend` on every run of this stage, on rocm10 and rocm724 and on several different MI355X runners:\r\n\r\n```\r\nUCX  ERROR   no active messages transport to <no debug data>: self/memory - no peer failure handler,\r\n  sysv/memory - no peer failure handler, posix/memory - no peer failure handler,\r\n  ud_verbs/rdma0:1 - Destination is unreachable, rocm_copy/rocm_cpy - no am bcopy, ...\r\nnixl._bindings.nixlBackendError: NIXL_ERR_BACKEND\r\n```\r\n\r\nExample: [job](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39665749264/job/119461271763). The test passed on the same image earlier on Oct 21, at a main commit before #43482 ([run](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39550230191)).\r\n\r\n#43482 maps `--disaggregation-ib-device` to the NIXL UCX `device_list`. NIXL applies that with `config.modifyAlways(\"NET_DEVICES\", \"rdma0:1\")`, which overrides the `UCX_NET_DEVICES` that the fixture sets. That drops `lo`. As the fixture comment in `_maybe_set_ucx_net_devices` notes, NIXL opens an endpoint to itself during `createBackend`, and on these RoCE NICs tcp over `lo` is the only transport that can serve it, because UD loopback on rdma0 is unreachable.\r\n\r\n## Notes for the reviewer\r\n\r\nThis puts the test back on the exact UCX device set it used before #43482, so it still runs over rdma0/rdma4.\r\n\r\nIt doesn't change #43482's behavior for real deployments. NIXL with `--disaggregation-ib-device` on a RoCE host without UD loopback will hit the same `createBackend` failure. That is worth a separate look, for example keeping `lo` or honoring an existing `UCX_NET_DEVICES`. I left it out of this PR.\r\n\r\n## Test plan\r\n\r\n- [x] Disaggregation stage on this commit: `test_nixl_transfer_engine_e2e.py` passes on rocm724 ([run](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39687286547)) and rocm10 ([run](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39687291939)). Both runs are 3/4: `test_disaggregation_pp.py` failed with intermittent Mooncake `KVTransferError`s during KV transfer. That test runs on Mooncake, not NIXL, and showed the same failures before this change.\r\n",
      "changedFiles": 1,
      "comments": {
