            },
            "body": "@Jzz1943 since #43482, `--disaggregation-ib-device` becomes NIXL's UCX `device_list`, which replaces `UCX_NET_DEVICES` and drops `lo`. On AMD RoCE NICs NIXL's self-endpoint then has no transport, and `createBackend` fails with `NIXL_ERR_BACKEND`. This PR keeps the AMD e2e test off that path. The same failure can hit real deployments on hosts like this. Could you take a look at whether the device_list mapping should keep `lo` or respect an existing `UCX_NET_DEVICES`?\n",
            "createdAt": "2026-10-21T23:02:54Z",
            "databaseId": 6328493442,
            "updatedAt": "2026-10-21T23:02:54Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/45674#issuecomment-6328493442"
          },
