  "inline_comments": [],
  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "@Jzz1943 since #43482, `--disaggregation-ib-device` becomes NIXL's UCX `device_list`, which replaces `UCX_NET_DEVICES` and drops `lo`. On AMD RoCE NICs NIXL's self-endpoint then has no transport, and `createBackend` fails with `NIXL_ERR_BACKEND`. This PR keeps the AMD e2e test off that path. The same failure can hit real deployments on hosts like this. Could you take a look at whether the device_list mapping should keep `lo` or respect an existing `UCX_NET_DEVICES`?\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-21T23:02:54Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/45674#issuecomment-6328493442",
      "id": 6328493442,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-21T23:02:54Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "michaelzhang-ai"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "@michaelzhang-ai Thanks for catching this and providing the CI evidence. I checked the NIXL code: device_list overrides NET_DEVICES, dropping the configured loopback interface. Simply adding lo to device_list would not work because NIXL appends :1. I’ll investigate a follow-up fix to preserve explicit UCX configuration while retaining per-GPU selection where supported. Could you help validate it on the affected AMD runners?\r\n\r\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-22T02:21:12Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/45674#issuecomment-6331130710",
      "id": 6331130710,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-22T02:21:12Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "Jzz1943"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "@michaelzhang-ai, I opened #45722 to preserve explicit UCX_NET_DEVICES over CLI device selection. Per-GPU selection remains supported when it is unset or empty. Could you help validate this on the affected AMD runners? Thanks!",
      "created_at": "2026-10-22T03:11:49Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/45674#issuecomment-6331751266",
      "id": 6331751266,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-22T03:11:49Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "Jzz1943"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Closing: #45722 fixes this at the source, and the AMD disaggregation stage passes on main with it.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-22T16:43:08Z",
